  "caption": "Quinn moved rowing indoors for winter, planned an hour on the erg, and met a rounded back and grumpy ribs by minute 42.\n\nRowing loads the lower back thousands of times a week, and long, tired pieces can let technique slip. Sudden changes, like a new season or switching indoors, are common times for aches to build.\n\nWhat often helps: break up long erg sessions or swap some for cycling, build hip and trunk strength, change load, rigging or blades one at a time, and eat enough to match your training.\n\nRib pain with deep breaths, coughing or sneezing should be assessed rather than rowed through. Back pain with numbness, leg weakness or constant night pain needs a same-day check.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
